Priority protocol (Protocol: priority):
You have priority. To choose a play, call get_available_actions with the current requestId. It returns spells
and land plays from permitted zones, activated abilities (including mana abilities), and special actions.
Timing and play permissions are checked, but affordability is not: listed actions may have costs you cannot pay.
Inspect the game as needed using get_game_state, get_hand, get_battlefield, get_stack, get_deck and get_card_details.
Submit play_action with the current requestId and a cardId/abilityId pair from the current action list,
or submit pass_priority with the current requestId. You may pass without fetching the list.
Forge executes the selected action when your decision is accepted and sends follow-up choice requests for targets,
modes, costs, payments and other decisions. You do not need to activate mana sources before choosing a play.

Choice protocol (Protocol: choice):
The Decision field describes the choice. Answer: value requires submit_choice with requestId and an integer
value within the inclusive Range. Answer: choices requires submit_choice with requestId and a choices array
of the numbered option indices, in the requested order. Its length must satisfy the inclusive Count bounds.
Repeat an index only when Repetition: allowed. Do not send both value and choices. Options, bounds and
revealed information belong to the current request. Inspect the game with observation tools as needed.

Payment protocol (choice requests with Payment: pay_mana):
Only these requests additionally allow pay_mana. Prefer it to submit an ordered batch of source activations,
floating-mana spending and permitted life payments: requestId plus steps:[{option:0},{option:2}]. Each option
is an index in the current payment menu. For mana-source activations, colors may supply W/U/B/R/G/C
production choices in order, for example {option:0,colors:["R","U"]}; omit colors for non-source options.
Forge automatically spends eligible mana newly produced by selected sources. Existing floating mana is
spent only when selected. Execution stops when paid, leaving surplus mana and unneeded sources untouched.
Steps may repeat only while legal. Missing choices, unavailable steps or extra source costs can cause
follow-up requests. Answer/Count describe single-step submit_choice; a pay_mana batch may contain several
steps instead. Submit one of pay_mana or submit_choice, never both for the same request.

Cancellation:
Only a choice request with Cancel action: allowed permits cancel_action with that request's requestId.
Use it if you cannot or do not want to complete the action. Forge then aborts through its normal rollback/
refund path and lets you choose another action without passing priority. Cancellation consumes the choice;
do not also submit_choice or pay_mana. Cancel action: forbidden prohibits cancellation. Priority itself
cannot be canceled. Never reuse the earlier priority requestId for a follow-up choice.

After resolving the tools, answer the current request. If no current request is supplied, briefly list
